id: vampire
name: Vampire
order: 10
category: body
# A Factor Trait replaces a Secondary Racial Trait - Secondary, then, unless it names a Primary one to replace.
importance: secondary
# (2)
grantsTalentIfManeuver: soar=frequent-flyer
# (3)
grantsUnique: shapeshift
uniqueRestrictions: specific-form
# (4)
grantsOther: monstrous, bestial
grantsOtherFrom: feast, fangs
grantsOtherOptions: fangs=savage
description: >
  Sustaining your unlife by draining the vitality of other beings, you are able to turn into a bat.
text: >
  Vampire (Body): Sustaining your unlife by draining the vitality of other beings, you are able to turn into a bat.
  (1)-[Passive]: You are Unnatural.
  (2)-[Passive]: You gain access to the Soar Maneuver. If you already have access to the Soar Maneuver, gain access to the Frequent Flyer Talent.
  (3)-[Passive]: You gain access to the Shapeshift Unique Ability, but it possesses the Specific Form Restriction (Small Size Category and Winged Beast Bestial Trait).
  (4)-[Passive]: You gain access to the Feast Monstrous Trait and the Fangs Bestial Trait (you must select the Savage effect for its Option effect).
  (5)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you would regain Life Points, except through a Surge, increase the amount of Life Points regained by your Surgency.
  (6)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you deal Damage with an Attacking Maneuver, you may use the Bite Special Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.

---

# (2) Frequent Flyer, where the Soar was had already as this is gained; (3) Shapeshift with Specific Form - the Small Size Category and
# Winged Beast, its Form the player's to keep to; (4) Feast, and Fangs with Savage - not asked. All its headers.
[passive]
# (1), (2)
allow unnatural;
allow maneuver.soar;
# (5) Life Points regained but through a Surge: asked once they are written, once a Round - your Surgency more (combat.mjs).
allow vampire.feed;
# (6) Damage dealt by your attack: the Bite Attack offered on its card at them, once a Round (chat.mjs vampireBite).
allow vampire.bite;
